  "status": "active",
  "activeSince": "2019",
  "lineage": "Operated by the TA505/FIN11 cybercrime cluster",
  "summary": "Cl0p began as a CryptoMix-derived encryptor deployed after TA505 phishing (Get2/SDBot/FlawedAmmyy/TrueBot) but since 2020 specialises in mass zero-day exploitation of managed file-transfer and ERP platforms (Accellion FTA, GoAnywhere, MOVEit, Cleo, Oracle E-Business Suite) for data-theft-only extortion. Web shells such as DEWMODE and LEMURLOOT pull data from the application database; encryption is now rare.",
  "uniqueTraits": [
    "Serial zero-day mass exploitation of file-transfer/ERP platforms: Accellion FTA (2020), GoAnywhere CVE-2023-0669, MOVEit CVE-2023-34362, Cleo CVE-2024-50623/CVE-2024-55956, Oracle EBS CVE-2025-61882",
    "Purpose-built web shells (DEWMODE, LEMURLOOT human2.aspx) that query application databases",
    "Encryption-less extortion via emails to executives and leak-site/torrent publication",
    "Historical TA505 tooling: FlawedAmmyy RAT, SDBot, TrueBot, Cobalt Strike"
  ],
